It's usually possible to find non-cursed daggers pretty early.
They're much better than a scalpel, and a healer can get them to
Skilled, which is reasonable in the early game.  Try to find the best
ones you can. (Elvish are better than regular; Orcish are worse.)
Because they can be thrown as well as wielded, the skill slots aren't
wasted when you switch to a better melee weapon later.

That, however, brings up the question:  what better melee weapon
should a Healer plan on switching to later?  The wiki suggests a
unicorn horn or the Staff, but those are both two-handed, which can be
a pain.  Most of the really good neutral artifacts aren't weapons, and
most of the really good artifact weapons aren't neutral.  (I don't
know all the Slash'em-specific stuff, though, so I could easily be
missing some other option.)  A crysknife presents certain annoying
maintenance headaches but may still be the best option if you want to
be at least Skilled.  Can a Healer wish for and use the Bat?  That
could make the club skill worth advancing.


